[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/dialogue/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n2_anselm"
text = "# DRAFT
# Anselm by the infirmary brazier at dusk (night 2). He heard the merchant carried past his door, or heard him leave cursing.
# The knock with no one there frightens him more than anything; it's new to him. He hints at his guilt and won't tell.
== start
(Anselm in his chair by the brazier. He turns his face toward your step before you speak.)
-> dead [if died_merchant]
-> lived [if n1_merchant=admitted]
-> plain

== dead
Anselm: They carried a man past my door this morning. Wet. I heard it run off him onto the flags.
(His voice drops.)
Anselm: Did you lock the door, porter? I told you. I told you to.
-> topics

== lived
Anselm: I heard your merchant in the court this morning, cursing you for locking him in.
(He's nearly smiling.)
Anselm: Let him curse. Let them all curse you, and go home.
-> topics

== plain
Anselm: The porter. You came through your first night. (He reaches for your hand, and holds it a moment.)
-> topics

== again
Anselm: Still there? I can hear you breathing.
-> topics

== topics
* [if n1_knock_no_one] [if not n2_anselm_knock] Last night there was a knock at the gate, and no one there. -> knock
* [if not n2_anselm_lost] In your years at the gate, brother, did you ever lose a guest? -> lost

== knock [set n2_anselm_knock]
(His hands find the arms of his chair and hold on.)
Anselm: And nobody there. In thirty years at that gate I never had that.
Anselm: Pray, porter. It's all I know to tell you.
-> topics

== lost [set n2_anselm_lost]
(A long silence. His hands tighten on the arms of the chair.)
Anselm: I'm blind, porter. I don't see anything now.
Anselm: I don't see anything.
-> topics

== leave
Anselm: Lock them in, porter.
"
